 "name": "HDA benzene plant — CHEMCAD-validated case",
 "description": "Toluene hydrodealkylation with gas and toluene recycles, rebuilt from the maintainer's CHEMCAD 8.1 design case (KMM4125 design project; stream and equipment numbers as in CHEMCAD). CHEMCAD models the reactor as two stoichiometric reactors in series (units 6 and 7, stream 8 between them); here it is one reactor with both reactions, as in the design drawing. Specifications (temperatures, pressures, 75 % toluene conversion, 2 % benzene to biphenyl in the same reactor, 15 % purge, column key recoveries) are read from the CHEMCAD stream table; pump efficiencies are back-calculated from its enthalpies. The columns are FUG shortcut designs with a reflux drum at 50 °C for the benzene column. The two recycle streams carry rounded start estimates. Property method SRK, which reproduces the CHEMCAD stream table best (PR was tested too). See docs/VALIDATION.md.",
